From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ned <github@edoardo.fyi>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 22:13:48 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 29/96] IOP: forward pending loads into LWL/LWR merges

Reproduce the lost-byte bug with LWR t0,1(a0); LWL t0,4(a0); nop over bytes 11 22 33 44 55. The new test failed before the fix; both pair orders now produce 0x55443322. Cover unaligned offsets, same and different pending destinations, and ordinary ALU/store/overwrite load delays.

Only the LWL/LWR merge operand reads a matching pending load. Address calculation and ordinary instruction operands retain their load delays.

Verified with ./tz build, ./tz test (54/54), ./tz test --full (1106 VU runs, zero mismatches/rejected), ./tz run --seconds 60 (title, zero underruns, no crash), and ./tz run --route first-mission (25.2 fps_dispfb2, zero VU fallbacks and steady audio underruns, no crash). Supplied baseline: 25.1 FPS; this is a correctness fix, with no measured A/B performance claim.

diff --git a/ps2xIOP/src/emulator/core/iop_cpu.cpp b/ps2xIOP/src/emulator/core/iop_cpu.cpp
index 21c2a8ecf4d561de8c7b23e86add6f9e9fcb2d04..3dc9a6859c953ae806bf6d9314389c894fa2e72a 100644
--- a/ps2xIOP/src/emulator/core/iop_cpu.cpp
+++ b/ps2xIOP/src/emulator/core/iop_cpu.cpp
@@ -368,7 +368,7 @@ namespace ps2x::iop::detail
         {
             const uint32_t address = cpu.gpr[rs] + static_cast<uint32_t>(simm);
             const uint32_t memory = m_memory.read32(address & ~3u);
-            const uint32_t old = cpu.gpr[rt];
+            const uint32_t old = cpu.pendingLoad && cpu.pendingLoadReg == rt ? cpu.pendingLoadValue : cpu.gpr[rt];
             static constexpr uint32_t masks[4] = {0x00FFFFFFu, 0x0000FFFFu, 0x000000FFu, 0x00000000u};
             static constexpr uint32_t shifts[4] = {24u, 16u, 8u, 0u};
             load(rt, (old & masks[address & 3u]) | (memory << shifts[address & 3u]));
@@ -389,7 +389,7 @@ namespace ps2x::iop::detail
         {
             const uint32_t address = cpu.gpr[rs] + static_cast<uint32_t>(simm);
             const uint32_t memory = m_memory.read32(address & ~3u);
-            const uint32_t old = cpu.gpr[rt];
+            const uint32_t old = cpu.pendingLoad && cpu.pendingLoadReg == rt ? cpu.pendingLoadValue : cpu.gpr[rt];
             static constexpr uint32_t masks[4] = {0x00000000u, 0xFF000000u, 0xFFFF0000u, 0xFFFFFF00u};
             static constexpr uint32_t shifts[4] = {0u, 8u, 16u, 24u};
             load(rt, (old & masks[address & 3u]) | (memory >> shifts[address & 3u]));
diff --git a/ps2xIOP/tests/iop_import_tests.cpp b/ps2xIOP/tests/iop_import_tests.cpp
index 53a5116bf1e3a9ae1e8d5a71fb238bdb5692b770..238e3a91e4d0928f33a7ed7901b2bd7ba47f27ca 100644
--- a/ps2xIOP/tests/iop_import_tests.cpp
